  abstract  = {Differential equations with accretive (dissipative) right sides in a Banach space are studied in the present paper. The following questions are considered: unique solvability of the Cauchy problem and the existence of bounded, periodic, almost-periodic, and precompact solutions. Justification of the Krylov-Bogolyubov averaging principle is given under conditions of accretiveness (dissipativeness) of the right side. It is also shown that the accretive (dissipative) property is a necessary condition for exponential convergence of solutions to the left (to the right).},
