  abstract  = {We revisit the problem of approximating a multiple-input multiple-output p × m rational transfer function H(s) of high degree by another p × m rational transfer function \hat{H}(s) of much smaller degree, so that the H2-norm of the approximation error is minimized. We show that in the general case of higher-order poles in the reduced-order model, called the defective case, the stationary points of the H2-norm of the approximation error can still be characterized by tangential interpolation conditions. We also indicate that the sensitivity of the solution of this problem depends on the parameterization used.},
